    "body": "The indicated part of the document can be null, too, in case the fragment specifies a nonexistant element. In that case we should still set the document's target element to null. (This happens in my proposed spec text and in Gecko/Blink, but has been lost in translation here :smile:). \n\nSo there should be a line after this setting the target to null if the indicated part is null.\n",
